“Bytecode pattern converts behavior into a compact instruction set executed by a virtual machine, allowing dynamic and high-performance execution without changing source code.”

Pattern Structure (Very Important)
Client
  ↓
Bytecode Program (Instructions)
  ↓
Virtual Machine (Executor)
  ↓
Context (Runtime Data)


Instead of hard-coding logic using if-else or polymorphism, you:
    Convert logic into bytecode instructions
    Store them in a compact form
    Execute them using a Bytecode Interpreter / Virtual Machine

